cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its released checkpoints, please cite it."
title: "sourcetrace: open-set audio deepfake attribution with neural codec residuals (CORE)"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/pujariaditya/sourcetrace"
abstract: >-
  Attribute a synthetic speech clip to the generator that produced it, or reject
  it as a generator never seen in training. A frozen WavLM-Large front-end feeds
  a small gated head; the distinguishing ingredient is a neural-codec
  reconstruction residual, 33 numbers taken off the waveform the speech model
  never sees. On the MLAAD v5 family-level open-set protocol it reaches 0.50%
  FPR95 against a published 3.36%, and the abstention rule reports its own
  measured coverage rather than discrimination alone. All figures are
  single-seed point estimates.
authors:
  - family-names: Pujari
    given-names: Aditya
keywords:
  - audio-deepfake
  - source-tracing
  - open-set-recognition
  - neural-codec
  - encodec
  - wavlm
  - conformal-prediction
  - mlaad
  - stopa
